# Product Row Click

By default, **clicking the row of any product table opens View Product** for
that SKU. Icons, checkboxes, menus, size links, claim/verify buttons, and any
other control that already does a job keep doing that job.

## What this means on the surface

- Click the product name, photo, UPC, a status chip that is not a button, a
  date, or empty space on the row → go to View Product, already focused on
  that product.
- Click a checkbox, the ⋮ menu, the reports icon, a pack-size link, Reformulate,
  Review & Claim, Verify ingredients, or any other control → that control’s
  own action. The row click stands down.

## How it is wired

Shared module: `js/product-row-click.js`. It attaches itself (same pattern as
sortable headers and load-more). Import it next to `sortable-tables.js` /
`table-pagination.js`. Do not reimplement row-click per page.

Opt out of a table or row with `data-no-row-click` — only when the row is
genuinely not a product (ingredient moves, invoice lines, org/user rows).

## Rules for the agent

- Never leave a new product table with a dead row. If the row is a product,
  clicking it must open View Product unless the click landed on a control.
- Do not steal clicks from icons or existing actions. Skip `a`, `button`,
  inputs, the checkbox / ⋮ / reports columns, size links, and Material icons.
- Do not add a parallel “click the name only” link and call it done — the
  whole row is the hit target.
- Non-product lists (invoices, organizations, users, ingredients, audit,
  alerts) must not navigate to View Product.
